  "safety": {
    "_comment": "Phase A safety rules. Everyone gets the full check and the report always goes to the optometrist. A red flag = no lens suggestion, report marked URGENT. Emergency signs = short path (power of each eye + grid only), then urgent referral. Under childUnderAge with any minus power (SE at or below childMyopiaFromSeD) = referral only, tag CHILD_MYOPIA. DRAFT: optometrist review needed.",
    "emergencySigns": ["SUDDEN_VISION_LOSS", "CURTAIN_SHADOW", "NEW_FLASHES"],
    "unspecifiedIsEmergency": true,
    "childUnderAge": 18,
    "childMyopiaFromSeD": -0.25,
    "shortPathSteps": ["POWER", "AMSLER"],
    "shortPathMinutes": 2
  },

  "lensAssisted": {
    "_comment": "Phase B over-refraction. Power = -1/d: for a strong eye the blur point is very close and 1 cm is about 0.18 D at -4.25 D. From triggerSeD (blur point under about 27 cm) staff hold a known minus lens about suggestOffsetD weaker (rounded towards the weaker lens to suggestStepD: -4.25 -> -2.00, -6.00 -> -4.00) and the test is repeated through it. Total = lens (vertex-corrected from vertexFromAbsD for a vertexDistanceM hold) + residual. No blur point within maxReachM = lens too strong, use a weaker one. From highMyopiaBeyondSeD the optometrist must confirm.",
